# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit a real key.

# --- NL to Cedar compiler backend (ADR-040) -------------------------------------
# Which model serves the compiler. Unset means: Gemini if GEMINI_API_KEY is present,
# else Groq if GROQ_API_KEY is present, else the local Ollama model — so a machine with
# no key at all still runs.
#
#   gemini  hosted. Preferred of the two hosted options: its free quota is metered in
#           requests per day (1,500) rather than tokens per day, so an evaluation run
#           costs ~30 requests instead of half a budget. NOTE: Google's *unpaid* tier
#           may use submitted content to improve their products, and what is submitted
#           is the operator's policy text. Fine for a prototype, not for a customer.
#   groq    hosted. Fast, but the free tier caps at 100,000 tokens per DAY — roughly
#           55 compiles, and one 30-case evaluation run spends over half of it.
#   ollama  strictly local, no egress, no third-party data exposure. The production
#           destination. Requires `ollama pull qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_0`.
AGENTIAM_LLM_BACKEND=gemini

# Put real values in `.env`, never here — this file IS tracked (see the `!.env.example`
# negation in .gitignore), so a key written here goes to the repository.

# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=
